meta {
  name: POST /api/trucks/{truckId}/fuel-card (IOCL)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/trucks/:truckId/fuel-card?provider=IOCL&alternateMobileNumber=
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  provider: IOCL
  alternateMobileNumber: 
}

params:path {
  truckId: 9901
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{adminStaticToken}}
}

docs {
  `TruckResource.createFuelCard` (plutus-java `common/controller/TruckResource.java:389`), called as VAHN_ADMIN.
  Real external write: creates the IOCL customer (if the truck's PAN has none) and the card.
  - Set `alternateMobileNumber` to the driver's number; leaving it blank clears the driver's alternate phone.
  - The IOCL customer mobile comes from the truck PAN's `pan_card.phone`, not from this param.
  Errors come back as HTTP 500 with `message: "Failed to create fuel card"`; the real cause is in the plutus logs.
}
